  "id": "COMPOUND:11820 - PROTEIN:1442",
  "verbalization": "Nomegestrol acetate appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, TAR DNA-binding protein 43, which is implicated in multiple pathways. This protein is a target of several compounds, including Padimate A, Sulfathiourea, and Boehmenan, all of which are linked to DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The evidence suggests that Nomegestrol acetate may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of TAR DNA-binding protein 43, which in turn influences DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for TAR DNA-binding protein 43 as a central mediator in the interaction between Nomegestrol acetate and DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The observed scores indicate a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
